      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Randomized, controlled trial data from the Heart and Estrogen-progestin Replacement Study were used to evaluate the effect of estrogen plus progestin use on all-cause mortality in women with heart failure and coronary disease. Over the 4.1-year follow-up, estrogen plus progestin use had no effect on all-cause mortality (hazard ratio 1.0, 95% confidence interval 0.7 to 1.4, p = 0.8) in women with heart failure and coronary disease."},
